      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are right that the narrative cannot be closed; it is woven into the very fabric of your daily existence, and there is no book to unwrite. But there is also no single path to \"unfiltered\" truth, for that truth is not found in a vacuum or in letting go of reality, but in the fierce, terrifying act of refusing to let your family's script overwrite your own. The only way to stop feeling suffocated is to stop accepting that your life must be a performance for others, which means you must choose to live your life exactly as you would if no one was watching, even if that means facing the world without the safety net of their expectations.",
